Z||000000||frontal lobe||07-21-2000||01:29 AM||||Wow, what a week!  You will NEVER guess what car I just got done driving.  Don't even bother.  You'll never get it.  Those of you that guessed anyway, wrong, wrong, all wrong (a local radio quiz person used to say that.)<P>A 1952 MG TD!!!!!  Mint condition.  Frame off restoration.  Unbelievable shape.  My friend inherited it from his deceased father-in-law who commissioned the restoration.  He brought it over to give me a ride, and then let me drive it.  Funny thing about driving it, though.  I kept wanting to say, "Pip, pip, cheerio, and all that jolly rot.  What say, Reginald?"  And his name isn't even Reginald, it's Clay.  Here's another thing that was funny.  Nobody had any Grey Poupon!  I know, I asked.  OK, I really didn't.<P>Seriously, you would not believe the number of people of all ages shouting "nice car".  A real attention magnet.<P>Not much of a daily driver around here, though, since I live in Siberia, USA (also known as Wisconsin).||||reg||1
